# Hero film sources.
#
# Two cuts of the same camera move — ScrollScrub picks between them by
# viewport shape. A 16:9 film under object-cover on a phone crops away most
# of its width, so portrait viewports get a natively vertical cut instead.
#
# Preferred (production): self-host both. Download the renders, run each
# through scripts/encode-scrub.sh, drop the output in apps/web/public/hero/,
# then set:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_FILM=/hero/scrub.mp4
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_FILM_PORTRAIT=/hero/scrub-portrait.mp4
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_POSTER=/hero/scrub-poster.jpg
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_POSTER_PORTRAIT=/hero/scrub-portrait-poster.jpg
#
# The encode step forces every frame to be a keyframe. Without it, seeking
# snaps to the nearest keyframe and the scrub visibly judders.
#
# If unset, the app falls back to the Higgsfield CDN URLs baked into
# app/page.tsx — fine for a preview, not for production.

NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_FILM=
NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_FILM_PORTRAIT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_POSTER=
NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_POSTER_PORTRAIT=
